        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96150?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Factor out Deferred Fetch documentation from the main \"Fetch API\" page.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">After this change, we now show a \"Baseline: Widely Available\" banner on the \"Fetch API\" page, and a \"Baseline: Limited Availability\" banner on the \"Using Deferred Fetch\" page.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43479.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4089524289\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43479\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43479/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43479\">#43479</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43480",
            "title": "Factor out Deferred Fetch documentation, shows Baseline on Fetch API",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-17T22:43:45.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-17T16:18:57.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dfabulich",
                "url": "https://github.com/dfabulich"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96150?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">These pages were referencing the <code class=\"notranslate\">browser-compat</code> data for the deprecated <code class=\"notranslate\">api.Document.fullscreen</code> feature, which doesn't have a corresponding feature ID in <code class=\"notranslate\">web-features</code>. As a result, these pages weren't displaying a Baseline banner.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">By removing that key from <code class=\"notranslate\">browser-compat</code>, the features will show the correct Baseline status banner.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43478",
            "title": "Add Baseline banner to Fullscreen API pages",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-17T15:52:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-17T15:50:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dfabulich",
                "url": "https://github.com/dfabulich"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/259028460?u=76c93f0df0fbeb4706736acca78f07a43e398a63&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a clarification explaining the difference between <code class=\"notranslate\">Document.querySelector()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Element.querySelector()</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This distinction is a common source of confusion for developers. The documentation previously did not clearly explain the scope difference between these two methods. This update helps readers better understand how each method works in practice.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">No functional changes. This is a documentation improvement with a simple example to illustrate the difference.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43367.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4040672682\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43367\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43367/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43367\">#43367</a><br>\nRelates to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4040672682\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43367\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43367/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43367\">#43367</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43476",
            "title": "docs: clarify difference between Document.querySelector() and Element.querySelector()",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-17T13:49:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-17T13:48:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dsk-dev-ai",
                "url": "https://github.com/dsk-dev-ai"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/259028460?u=76c93f0df0fbeb4706736acca78f07a43e398a63&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43427.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4069573538\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43427\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43427/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43427\">#43427</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR clarifies the terminology used for \"stylesheet\" in the glossary.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">MDN commonly uses the one-word form \"stylesheet\", while official specifications such as those from the W3C use the two-word form \"style sheet\".</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This update keeps MDN’s convention while acknowledging both forms to improve clarity and consistency.</p>",
