        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141215061?u=a9271c92151c7a29629057e254a5699c551496b5&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds an Accessibility section to the CSS Custom Highlight API page.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Summarizes the intended behavior from the specification: the type attribute can be used by user agents to expose semantic meaning (such as spelling or grammar errors) to assistive technologies.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Notes that current support is limited and inconsistent across browsers and platform accessibility APIs.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Provides guidance for developers: custom highlights should not be relied on alone to convey important information; semantic HTML elements like <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;mark&gt;</code> or additional accessible cues should be used when highlighting conveys meaning.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This update ensures that developers are aware of accessibility limitations and helps prevent assumptions about screen reader support.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43408.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4058808289\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43408\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43408/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43408\">#43408</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43469",
            "title": "add accessibility section for CSS Custom Highlight API",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-17T11:24:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-17T11:22:50.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "mohammed-ali-osman",
                "url": "https://github.com/mohammed-ali-osman"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF149 adds support for the shorthand CSS property <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-box\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">text-box</code></a> , corresponding longhand properties <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-box-trim\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">text-box-trim</code></a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-box-edge\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">text-box-edge</code></a>, and the value <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/text-edge\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">text-edge</code></a> behind the preference <code class=\"notranslate\">layout.css.text-box.enabled</code> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2013458\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2013458</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds an experimental features entry and a release note entry that are essentially the same.<br>\nTried to catch a flavour of what this does, which is make it possible to align text within a box so that it is visually positioned consistently for different fonts.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3977998210\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43208\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43208/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43208\">#43208</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43468",
            "title": "FF149 ExprFeat/Relnote: CSS text-box and longhand props",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-18T11:18:10.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-17T05:42:34.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This updated does two things.</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Updates the \"Using container size and style queries\" doc to:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Update legacy note that only style queries with custom properties are supported. I believe all the types are - certainly that is what the <code class=\"notranslate\">@container</code> docs indicate and the BCD seems to show.</li>\n<li>Link the Container style queries intro to the more detailed section on <code class=\"notranslate\">@container</code> doc.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Adds a note in <code class=\"notranslate\">@container</code> docs that <code class=\"notranslate\">!important</code> is allowed in style queries but ignored. This apparently is not clear in the spec but is in a <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-conditional/container-queries/at-container-style-parsing.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">WPT test that is passed by all browsers</a>. This came up in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2014095\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2014095</a> and I think is worthy of a mention.</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3978087686\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43216\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43216/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43216\">#43216</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43466",
            "title": "FF149 @container style() allows but ignores !important",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-17T03:30:06.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-17T03:28:16.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218712309?u=25fee3155ae1576e7584c863372db035549e7bd9&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updated the text in the \"Functions are called with the global <code class=\"notranslate\">this</code>\" section of the <code class=\"notranslate\">setInterval</code> page. Removed the incorrect claim about arrow functions using lexical <code class=\"notranslate\">this</code>, since the example just wraps the method call with dot notation.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The old text said the example demonstrates lexical <code class=\"notranslate\">this</code>, but it doesn't - the arrow function simply calls <code class=\"notranslate\">myArray.myMethod()</code> directly, which works because of dot notation, not lexical <code class=\"notranslate\">this</code>. This was confusing and technically incorrect.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43441.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4076308033\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43441\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43441/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43441\">#43441</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43465",
            "title": "fix: Fix misleading lexical  claim in setInterval docs to match the actual example",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-18T00:35:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-17T02:07:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "bittoby",
                "url": "https://github.com/bittoby"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds reference docs for WebAssembly SIMD load instructions.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
